.TH "EPX\-AUTH" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-auth \- check Emporix credentials
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx auth [flags]
epx auth [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx auth status"
Request a token and show the tenant and scopes it grants.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx auth status [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Requests a service token for the tenant plus the given scopes and shows what was granted. Emporix grants only requested scopes, so pass \fB\-\-scope\fR to check specific permissions; a missing scope fails with exit code 3. The token itself is never printed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among TENANT, EXPIRES IN, SCOPES.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-scope <strings>\fR
Scope the credential must grant (repeatable).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx auth status \-\-scope product.product_read_unpublished \-\-scope indexing.search_view
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBepx\fR(1) for the global options, the credentials epx reads and its exit codes; https://commerce-cloud-integrations.github.io/emporix-cli/commands/auth
